[kutty] INTERPRETATION
===============================
TERMS: inside means earlier and outside means later. so load X is outside load Y means 
load Y was issued then load X was issued. 

Jump out means reorder with a latter instruction jump inside means reorder with an earlier 
instruction.

Good now lets see:

-> loads can jump below stores (respecting RAW)

-> no other memops are allowed to jump past each other for writeback mem

-> lfence allows stores to jump outside and none else

-> sfence allows loads to jump in and out

-> mfence allows no jumping past each other :-)

-> locked instructions dont allow any jumping past each other either
   <hence the adage of using lock:add [esp], 0 for lock acquires>

